  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A parallel plate capacitor <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi></math> with plates of unit area and separation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>d</mi></math> is filled with a liquid of dielectric constant <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math>, the level of liquid is<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo></math>initially.&nbsp;<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/bitsat/974c2e8a-cf06-4938-97ce-f4fba41c1918-image.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 183px;\" /><br />Suppose, the liquid level decreases at a constant speed <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi></math>, the time constant as a function of time is</p>",
